=== created .commandments/sessions/.names
-----
review	parity
-----
The names this project has given its sessions (`commandments session name "<name>"`). A session folder is a hash by default; a named one IS the name, and this says which id it belongs to so an agent can still find its own folder from the id it was given.

Between the dividers is the list: one `name<TAB>session-id` per line. The NAME is the folder under `sessions/`, and the id is what the harness calls the session it holds.

Safe to delete — a named session becomes findable by its hash again — nothing inside it is lost.

